          Light rises x7.8 in 0.12 s (steeper than 3x the air-density tracking rate). Associated with:
          yield gen 0 at 40.9 km (95% of m0); split gen 0 at 40.4 km (94% of m0). Dust groups supply
          53% of the rise and 46% of the light at the end of the flare. A real fragmentation flare
          (Phase 5 in [R22]); its sharpness and timing here come from the model's deterministic
          cascade.
    5  B   first_breakup            3.783    40.47   3.583e+09  stylized
